    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$3.97 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a vegetable heavy soup that still hits real protein numbers. The artichoke hearts and canned tomatoes are the two lines carrying the cost here.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eArtichoke hearts are the surprise expense.\u003c/strong\u003e Canned in water is cheaper than marinated in oil and works better in a soup, since you are not paying for oil you drain away.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned diced tomatoes go on sale constantly.\u003c/strong\u003e This recipe uses a lot of them. Buy a case when the price drops and you will use every can within a month.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFresh basil is the smallest quantity for the biggest price.\u003c/strong\u003e Dried oregano is already carrying the herb weight. Treat the basil as optional if the board shows it high.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eChickpeas and green beans are the cheapest volume in the pot.\u003c/strong\u003e That is exactly how minestrone was designed to work, and it is why this feeds fourteen."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Dice the celery and onion, mince the garlic, drain and quarter the artichoke hearts, and drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
                    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot and brown the hot Italian sausage in crumbles until it takes on color.",
                    "Add the celery and onion and cook until they soften, then add the garlic and the dried oregano for a minute.",
                    "Pour in the diced tomatoes and the beef broth, season with salt and black pepper, and bring it up to a simmer.",
                    "Add the green beans, the artichoke hearts and the chickpeas and simmer until the vegetables are tender.",
                    "Stir in the pasta shells and cook only until they are just tender. Overcooked pasta turns to paste after a night in the fridge, and this soup is meant to be reheated.",
                    "Fold in the chopped fresh basil off the heat and stir the parmesan through right before you portion."
                ],
